#
# Build context of the builder image (containers/builder/Dockerfile).
#
# The context is this repository, not containers/builder/, because
# west.yml and patches/ are image inputs since r3 — the image bakes a west
# workspace and applies the patch set into it. The Dockerfile copies four
# things and nothing else (west.yml, patches/, containers/builder/
# requirements.txt, containers/builder/workspace-record.py), so this file
# is about keeping the context small and reproducible rather than about
# secrecy: the whole repository is ~6 MB, 2 MB of which is .git.
#
# Excluded is everything that is either large, machine-local, or output.
# Note what is NOT excluded: the C sources, the components and the docs.
# Listing them would be one more thing to keep in step with the
# Dockerfile's COPY lines, for no measurable gain at this size.

.git
.github

# Build and test output — machine-local, sometimes gigabytes.
build/
build_*/
twister-out*/
dist/

# Python and tool caches; a __pycache__ from another interpreter version
# is exactly the kind of thing that makes two contexts differ for no
# reason.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
